{{box cssClass="floatinginfobox" title="**Contents**"}}
{{toc/}}
{{/box}}

Personal bookmarks for XWiki users, stored with their account rather than in their browser: a star on every page, folders and subfolders in a management page, a quick-access panel, and export and import. Bookmarks are private: only their owner and the administrators of the wiki can see and change them.

[[image:management.png||alt="Management page of Advanced Bookmarks"]]

= Features =

* **Star**: a star button in the action bar of every page (next to //Edit// and //Create//) adds the page to the bookmarks of the current user, or removes it.
* **Panel**: the //Bookmarks// panel lists the bookmarks selected by the user, or the first ones, with a link to the management page.
* **Management page**: folders and subfolders, ordered freely by drag and drop or with the keyboard (arrow buttons and //Move to// lists), inline renaming, selection of the bookmarks displayed in the panel, and a filter. Changes are saved automatically.
* **Space used indicator**: shows how much of the space allowed for the bookmarks is used, and warns when it is almost full.
* **Profile tab**: the same management interface in a //Bookmarks// tab of the user profile.
* **Export and import**: users save their bookmarks to a JSON file, and add such a file to their bookmarks or restore it. Administrators can also export and import the bookmarks of all the users of a wiki.
* **Pages followed automatically**: when a page is renamed or moved, its bookmarks are updated; a deleted page stays in the bookmarks, struck through.
* **Configuration for each wiki**: size of the panel, display of the star, pages that cannot be bookmarked.
* **Administrator help**: administrators can open and manage the bookmarks of any user of their wiki, for support.
* English and French translations.

= Prerequisites =

* XWiki 17.10.2 or later, running on Java 17 or later.
* Solr embedded in XWiki (the default), or a remote Solr server in which an administrator creates the core of the extension (see [[Storage and backup>>||anchor="HStorageandbackup"]]).

= Installation =

Install the **Advanced Bookmarks** extension ({{{org.xwiki.contrib.advancedbookmarks:advanced-bookmarks-ui}}}) with the Extension Manager. Its Java part, {{{advanced-bookmarks-api}}}, is installed automatically.

* **Farm level**: the Java part can only be installed on the whole farm. The Solr core it creates is shared by all the wikis of the farm, and XWiki creates Solr cores from the components installed at farm level. Installing an extension on the whole farm requires programming rights.
* **Installing user**: install as an administrator of the wiki. The star is only displayed when the author of its UI extension has the administration right, and the features reserved to administrators (managing the bookmarks of other users, administration tools) also require that the author of the page running them administers the wiki. If the installing account later loses this right, reinstall the extension, or save its pages again, as an administrator.
* **Panel**: the panel is not added to the page layout automatically. Add {{{Panels.MyBookmarks}}} in //Administration > Look & Feel > Panels//.
* **Upgrades**: upgrading replaces a farm-level JAR, after which XWiki reloads the other farm-level JAR extensions. Some of them may log warnings or errors during this reload, and an extension whose components fail to reload stays partly inactive until XWiki is restarted. Plan upgrades with a restart of XWiki.

Before the first installation, back up the permanent directory of XWiki: the extension creates a Solr core.

= Usage =

== Star ==

Logged-in users see a star in the action bar of each page. Clicking it adds the page to the //Uncategorized// bookmarks, or removes it. The star is not displayed on excluded pages (see [[Configuration>>||anchor="HConfiguration"]]), nor on the pages of the extension itself.

[[image:star.png||alt="Star in the action bar of a page"]]

== Panel ==

The panel displays the bookmarks selected with the //Panel// box of the management page, up to the configured panel size (10 by default). Without any selection, it displays the first bookmarks, in the order of the management page. Deleted pages are struck through; pages the user cannot view are shown without a link.

[[image:panel.png||alt="Bookmarks panel"]]

== Management page ==

The page {{{AdvancedBookmarks.WebHome}}} (//View all my bookmarks// in the panel) displays the {{{{{bookmarks/}}}}} macro, which can also be used in any other page. Users can:

* create folders and subfolders, rename and delete them;
* move folders and bookmarks by drag and drop, with the arrow buttons, or with the //Move to// lists;
* rename a bookmark (its label), or remove it;
* select the bookmarks to display in the panel;
* filter the list by label, page or folder.

Changes are saved automatically. If the bookmarks were modified meanwhile (in another tab, or with the star), the page reloads them and tells the user.

The //Space used// indicator shows the share of the space allowed for the bookmarks that is used. It warns from 80% and tells that the bookmarks are almost full from 95% (see [[Limits>>||anchor="HLimits"]]).

Administrators also get a user picker: the bookmarks of the chosen user open in a new tab ({{{AdvancedBookmarks.WebHome?user=XWiki.jdoe}}}), with a banner recalling whose bookmarks are displayed.

The macro has an optional {{{user}}} parameter: {{{{{bookmarks user="XWiki.jdoe"/}}}}} displays the bookmarks of that user instead of the current one, provided the current user is allowed to see them.

== Profile tab ==

A //Bookmarks// tab is added to the user profile. It displays the same management interface for the user of the profile, and is only shown to that user and to the administrators of the wiki.

[[image:profile-tab.png||alt="Bookmarks tab of the user profile"]]

The tab needs the user profile of XWiki ({{{xwiki-platform-user-profile-ui}}}, installed by the standard flavor); without it, the tab is simply not displayed.

== Export and import ==

The //Export// button of the management page downloads the bookmarks as a JSON file. //Import…// reads such a file and, after confirmation, either:

* **adds it** to the current bookmarks: an imported folder is merged with the folder of the same name (ignoring case) at the same place, other folders are created, imported items come after the existing ones of their folder, and pages already bookmarked are skipped. Importing an export of the same bookmarks changes nothing;
* or **replaces** the current bookmarks with the content of the file.

Page references are exported without their wiki, so a file can be imported into another wiki or farm. Pages of another wiki, excluded pages and pages the user cannot view found in a file are skipped.

The export file has this format:

{{code language="json"}}
{"format": "advanced-bookmarks", "formatVersion": 1, "exportedAt": "2026-10-10T08:00:00Z",
 "folders": [{"id": "f1", "name": "Work", "parent": "", "order": 0}],
 "bookmarks": [{"page": "Sandbox.WebHome", "label": "", "folder": "f1", "order": 0, "panel": false}]}
{{/code}}

= Configuration =

Each wiki has its own settings, in //Administration > Other > Advanced Bookmarks// (stored in the page {{{AdvancedBookmarks.Code.Configuration}}} of the wiki). A wiki that has not been configured uses the defaults. Only the administrators of the wiki can change them.

|=Setting|=Default|=Description
|Panel size|10|Maximum number of bookmarks displayed in the panel, from 1 to 20. An invalid value is replaced by the default, with a warning in the logs. When it is lowered, the panels are shortened at once, and the extra selections are removed the next time each user saves their bookmarks.
|Display the star|Yes|Displays the star in the action bar of the pages. When it is hidden, bookmarks can only be added by importing a file.
|Excluded pages|None|Pages that may not be added to the bookmarks, with the star or by an import (at most 100), chosen in the page tree of the wiki. Selecting the home page of a space, such as {{{Main.Archives.WebHome}}}, also excludes all its child pages. Existing bookmarks of these pages are kept and can still be removed.

The pages of the extension itself (the {{{AdvancedBookmarks}}} space and {{{Panels.MyBookmarks}}}) are always excluded.

[[image:administration.png||alt="Administration section of Advanced Bookmarks"]]

= Administration tools =

The same administration section, above the settings, offers tools reserved to the administrators of the wiki:

* **Storage**: whether the {{{advancedbookmarks}}} Solr core can be queried. When it cannot, the cause is written to the server logs.
* **Export all the bookmarks**: downloads the bookmarks of all the users of the wiki as a single JSON file. Users whose bookmarks cannot be read are skipped and logged.
* **Import…**: imports such a file in the background, user by user, in the //add// or //replace// mode of the individual import, with a progress bar and a summary. The whole file is validated before anything is written: an invalid file changes nothing. Users of the file who do not exist in the wiki are skipped; a user whose bookmarks cannot be imported is counted as failed and logged, and the import goes on. Only one import of a wiki runs at a time.

The wiki export file has this format:

{{code language="json"}}
{"format": "advanced-bookmarks-wiki", "formatVersion": 1, "exportedAt": "2026-10-10T08:00:00Z",
 "users": [{"user": "XWiki.jdoe",
            "folders": [{"id": "f1", "name": "Work", "parent": "", "order": 0}],
            "bookmarks": [{"page": "Sandbox.WebHome", "label": "", "folder": "f1", "order": 0, "panel": false}]}]}
{{/code}}

Local users are written without their wiki, so that the file can be imported into another wiki; global users of a farm keep the main wiki prefix ({{{xwiki:XWiki.jdoe}}}), so that they stay global.

= Rights and privacy =

Bookmarks are private, and kept separately for each wiki of a farm. All the checks are made on the server:

* the current user and wiki always come from the XWiki context, never from the browser;
* users read and modify only their own bookmarks; the administrators of a wiki can also manage the bookmarks of any existing user of that wiki, provided the page running the operation was also written by an administrator, so that a script written by someone else cannot use the rights of an administrator viewing it;
* guests have no bookmarks;
* a page can only be bookmarked by a user who can view it, and live information about a bookmarked page (whether it exists, its URL) is only given to users who can view it;
* modifications are only accepted in POST requests carrying a valid CSRF token.

The extension does not require programming rights to run.

= Storage and backup =

The bookmarks are stored in a dedicated Solr core, {{{advancedbookmarks}}}: one document per user and wiki, holding the folders and bookmarks as JSON. The XWiki database is not used.

* With the Solr embedded in XWiki (the default), the extension creates the core automatically, in the permanent directory of XWiki.
* With a remote Solr server, an administrator must create the {{{advancedbookmarks}}} core before installing the extension, as for the Likes and Ratings applications.

**The core is not rebuilt from the XWiki database.** Include it in regular, consistent backups:

* embedded Solr: back up the Solr data under the permanent directory of XWiki, together with the database;
* remote Solr: back up the core with the backup procedure of the Solr server.

The export of the administration tools also gives a copy of the bookmarks of a whole wiki, which can be imported again.

= Limits =

|=Limit|=Value
|Size of the bookmarks of a user|32,766 bytes of JSON, about 150 to 300 bookmarks depending on the length of the page references and labels. This is the largest value the Solr field holding them accepts. Beyond it, saving, adding with the star or importing is refused with a message asking to remove bookmarks, and nothing is changed.
|Panel size|From 1 to 20 bookmarks (10 by default)
|Excluded pages|100 per wiki
|Folder name, bookmark label|100 and 200 characters
|Wiki export file|32 MB and 10,000 users

= Known limitations =

* **Renamed user page**: XWiki handles the renaming of a user page as the deletion of the old user, so the bookmarks of the old user are erased; they are not transferred to the new name. To keep them, an administrator exports them before the rename, from the management page opened for that user ({{{AdvancedBookmarks.WebHome?user=<old user>}}}, //Export//), then imports the file after the rename, from the management page opened for the new user (//Import…//, replace mode).
* **Global users of a farm**: bookmarks are kept for each wiki. The profile of a global user, which is on the main wiki, shows the bookmarks of the main wiki only.
* **Page moved to another wiki**: its bookmarks are not followed, and the page is displayed as deleted.
* When a user is deleted, their bookmarks are erased in every wiki. When a wiki is deleted, all its bookmarks are erased.

= Scripting API =

{{{$services.advancedbookmarks}}} returns maps ready to be serialized as JSON. Each result has a {{{status}}} key (an HTTP status code) and, on failure, an {{{error}}} key: {{{forbidden}}}, {{{invalidToken}}}, {{{methodNotAllowed}}}, {{{invalid}}}, {{{tooLarge}}} (the bookmarks would exceed their maximum size), {{{conflict}}} or {{{storageError}}}. Error details are only written to the server logs. Write operations only accept POST requests carrying a valid CSRF token in the {{{form_token}}} parameter.

|=Method|=Description
|{{{getBookmarks(user)}}}|Folders and bookmarks of a user (empty for the current user), in display order, with their {{{version}}}, the space they use ({{{size}}}, in bytes) and the space allowed ({{{maxSize}}}).
|{{{getPanel()}}}|Bookmarks of the current user selected for the panel, or the first ones, up to the configured panel size.
|{{{isBookmarked(page)}}}|Whether the current user bookmarked a page ({{{bookmarked}}}), and whether the page may be bookmarked ({{{bookmarkable}}}, {{{false}}} for an excluded page).
|{{{isStarEnabled()}}}|Whether the current wiki displays the star (a plain boolean).
|{{{toggle(page)}}}|Add the page to the uncategorized bookmarks of the current user, or remove it. Adding an excluded page is refused ({{{forbidden}}}). Write operation.
|{{{save(user, json, version)}}}|Replace all the bookmarks of a user, provided they were not modified since {{{version}}} was read; {{{conflict}}} otherwise. Adding a page that is excluded or that the user cannot view is refused ({{{forbidden}}}); pages already bookmarked are kept. Returns the new {{{version}}} and the space used ({{{size}}}). Write operation.
|{{{exportBookmarks(user)}}}|Export file of the bookmarks of a user, as a JSON string under the {{{content}}} key.
|{{{importBookmarks(user, json, mode, version)}}}|Import an export file in the {{{merge}}} or {{{replace}}} mode, provided the bookmarks were not modified since {{{version}}} was read. Returns the new {{{version}}} and the number of bookmarks {{{imported}}} and {{{skipped}}}. Write operation.

{{{$services.advancedbookmarks.admin}}} exposes the administration tools of the current wiki, with the same kind of results. Every method returns {{{forbidden}}} to users who do not administer the wiki.

|=Method|=Description
|{{{getStoreStatus()}}}|Whether the storage can be queried, under the {{{available}}} key.
|{{{exportWiki()}}}|Wiki export file under the {{{content}}} key, with the number of users {{{exported}}} and {{{skipped}}}.
|{{{startWikiImport(mode)}}}|Validate the wiki export file sent in the {{{file}}} part of the current {{{multipart/form-data}}} request, then import it in the background in the {{{merge}}} or {{{replace}}} mode. Returns the number of {{{users}}} of the file; {{{conflict}}} if an import of the wiki is already running. Write operation.
|{{{getWikiImportStatus()}}}|{{{state}}} of the running or last import ({{{none}}}, {{{running}}} or {{{finished}}}) and, unless {{{none}}}, its {{{progress}}} (percentage), the counts {{{importedUsers}}}, {{{skippedUsers}}}, {{{failedUsers}}}, {{{importedBookmarks}}} and {{{skippedBookmarks}}}, and {{{failed}}} if it stopped on an unexpected error.

The page {{{AdvancedBookmarks.Code.Service}}} exposes the same operations over HTTP, with the {{{get}}} action and an {{{operation}}} parameter ({{{isBookmarked}}}, {{{toggle}}}, {{{getBookmarks}}}, {{{save}}}, {{{export}}}, {{{import}}}, and for administrators {{{exportWiki}}}, {{{startWikiImport}}}, {{{wikiImportStatus}}}). It returns the result as JSON, with the matching HTTP status.